{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For we are about to destroy.</b> They should have said 'for YHWH is about to destroy,' but they attributed the action to themselves and did not depart from there until they were compelled against their will to acknowledge that the matter does not depend on them but that they are emissaries from before HaShem — this is why they needed to say, 'and HaShem has sent us to destroy it.' And this is what Scripture says (Job 4:18): ״הן בעבדיו לא יאמין ובמלאכיו ישים תהלה״. And it is written (Job 15:15): ״הן בקדושיו לא יאמין ושמים לא זכו בעיניו״. ״הן בקדושיו לא יאמין״ — these are the pious, the prophets, and the holy ones, of whom it is said (Psalms 16:3): ״לקדושים אשר בארץ המה״. And so we find with Moses our master, peace be upon him, who said (Deuteronomy 1:17): ״והדבר אשר יקשה מכם״ etc., and he was held in suspense regarding the punishment of this matter in the case of the daughters of Zelophehad. And so Samuel the prophet, peace be upon him, who said to Saul (I Samuel 9:19): ״אנכי הרואה״, and when he came to anoint David and saw Eliab, he said (I Samuel 16): ״אך נגד ה׳ משיחו״; the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״אל תביט אל מראהו״ etc., ״כי האדם יראה לעינים וה׳ יראה ללבב״. And so David, who said (Psalms 40:9): ״ותורתך בתוך מעי״, erred in a matter that even schoolchildren know. And so Deborah, who praised herself and said (Judges 5:7): ״עד שקמתי דבורה שקמתי אם בישראל״ — the holy spirit departed from her and she needed to say (ibid.): ״עורי עורי דבורה עורי עורי דברי שיר״. ״ובמלאכיו ישים תהלה״ — these are the angels who were sent to Sodom, who said, 'we are about to destroy'; because they grew proud and attributed the matter to themselves, they were banished from their station for 138 years. The explanation of this is that they were not sent again on an embassy of the Holy One, blessed be He, until Jacob, to whom they returned on His embassy, as it is said (Genesis 28:12): ״והנה מלאכי אלהים״ etc. And from the overthrow of Sodom — at which time Abraham our father was 99 years old — until these angels of Elohim came to Jacob, one finds 138 years. And this is what is written there: ״עולים ויורדים בו״, that is to say, those who went up at the overthrow of Sodom are now going down in it; and all this time they were punished and did not go on an embassy of the Place at all. From here there is a great punishment for one who attributes the glory of the Holy One, blessed be He, to himself, for the entire world and its fullness were created only for His glory, blessed be He, and it is not fitting to ascribe His glory to another."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:44.121741706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}